      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/3/85/4",
      "text": [
        " : «لَوْ أَنَّ رَجُلاً مُعْسِراً أَحَجَّهُ رَجُلٌ كَانَتْ لَهُ حَجَّةٌ فَإِنْ أَيْسَرَ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ كَانَ عَلَيْهِ اَلْحَجُّ وَ كَذَلِكَ اَلنَّاصِبُ إِذَا عَرَفَ فَعَلَيْهِ اَلْحَجُّ وَ إِنْ كَانَ قَدْ حَجَّ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2867 - Ali ibn Abi Hamzah narrated from Abu Basir, from Abu Abdullah (as), who said:\n\"If an impoverished man is sent for Hajj by another person, it will count as a Hajj for him. However, if he later becomes financially capable, Hajj will still be obligatory upon him. Similarly, a Nasibi (one who opposes the Ahlulbayt), if he comes to recognize the truth, Hajj becomes obligatory upon him, even if he had already performed it previously.\""
        ]
      }
    },
